# Covers: at (mytag.enter?) — the tag's enter event fires when a scope
#         prefixed with that tag is entered (OP_PUSH_TAG).
# matrix-row: tag-scope-events
#
# `t.enter` is a PROPERTY, not a method: reading it allocates the tag's
# enter event on first ask and hands it back, which is what lets
# `at (t.enter?)` name it.  A tag nobody ever subscribes to never
# allocates one, so entering and leaving its scope costs nothing.
#
# Activated with the reactive runtime; the pre-activation draft named
# `Realm.log` only because a closure could not see a top-level `var`.

var t = Tag.new("scope")
var log = ""
at (t.enter?) log = log + "in"
t: { 1 }
log
[00000000] <Tag: scope>
[00000000] ""
[00000000] nil
[00000000] 1
[00000000] "in"
